  "$comment": "Canonical shared-scaffold manifest consumed by scripts/sync_template_shared.py. Every path under files/ is copied byte-for-byte into each template's template/ directory, and every library/*.tmpl into each template's library/. A template listed in opt_out for a path does not receive it. CI runs the sync in --check mode, so editing a copy inside a template without editing the canonical file here fails the drift test. fork_reviews pins each opted-out fork to the sha256 of the canonical file it was last reviewed against: editing a canonical file that has forks fails --check until the change is reviewed against every fork and `python scripts/sync_template_shared.py --acknowledge-forks` re-pins the hashes. The pin is of the canonical, not the fork \u2014 a fork evolves freely, but a canonical change must be consciously dispositioned for each fork it cannot reach.",
